{# Where a request came from, as a page of the account writes it (architecture §3.5, §5.2): the place the
   enrichment found, the address it came from, and the browser its user agent names.

   One file for the two tables that show it, because what a person reads of a session and of a sign-in is
   the same thing. The place is unknown rather than absent: a deployment that downloaded no database of
   addresses, and an address no database can place, are the same answer to whoever reads the line, and a
   line that said nothing would read as a line nobody filled in. The browser is what the reading of the
   user agent recognises (Domain\Session\Device), and the whole of what the browser sent stays in the
   document, where somebody looking for exactly that can read it.

   A request without an address is the provider's own, its console or its schedule: its user agent names the
   command and the shell of the operator, which the person is not told (decision 0066).

   "provenance" is a RequestContext: the caller passes the one its row carries. #}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}
{% set place = provenance.location|beffroi_place %}
<span data-place="{{ place is not null ? 'known' : 'unknown' }}">{{ place ?? 'provenance.unknown_place'|trans }}</span>
{{ provenance.ipAddress ?? 'provenance.unknown_address'|trans }}
{% if provenance.userAgent is not null and provenance.ipAddress is not null %}
    <span data-user-agent title="{{ provenance.userAgent }}">{{ provenance|beffroi_device }}</span>
{% endif %}
